+    /*
+     * POMPPC tcg/0040 (x-dirty-skip).  An over-approximation of the entries
+     * tlb_reset_dirty() may have to change, i.e. those whose write side has
+     * none of TLB_INVALID_MASK, TLB_NOTDIRTY, TLB_MMIO, TLB_DISCARD_WRITE.
+     * Invariant, with tlb_c.lock held: every such entry of mmu_idx i (table
+     * or victim) has its host page in [lo, hi) of a slot whose idx has bit
+     * i, or bit i is set in dw_over.  Entries become such only in
+     * tlb_set_page_full() and tlb_set_dirty(), which record them; a whole
+     * flush of mmu_idx i clears bit i everywhere; tlb_reset_dirty() empties
+     * a slot whose range it has entirely reset.  One slot per RAMBlock, so
+     * the guest RAM and a frame buffer never share a range.  Within a slot,
+     * bm[i] (allocated on first use, POMPPC_DW_BITS bits) marks where the
+     * entries of mmu_idx i are: bit (index mod POMPPC_DW_BITS) for an entry
+     * at table index `index'.  An entry for page P is always at index
+     * tlb_index(P) of its table or in its victim TLB (a resize flushes the
+     * table), so the indices of the set bits, modulo the table size, and
+     * the victim TLB hold them all.  bm[i] is all zero when bit i of idx is
+     * clear.
+     */
